# Figma Layout Primitive Mapping

When translating Figma designs to code using `get_design_context`, map layout containers to kit primitives from the generated code's layout properties. Do not require designers to name layers after primitives.

Import layout from `@appdirect/ds-prototype-kit`.

## Decision Algorithm

### 1. Vertical stack (`flex-direction: column`)

```tsx
import { Stack } from '@appdirect/ds-prototype-kit';
<Stack gap="md">{children}</Stack>
```

### 2. Horizontal row (`flex-direction: row`)

```tsx
import { Inline } from '@appdirect/ds-prototype-kit';
<Inline gap="sm">{children}</Inline>
```

### 3. Grid

```tsx
import { Grid } from '@appdirect/ds-prototype-kit';
<Grid cols={{ base: 1, md: 2, lg: 3 }} spacing="lg">{children}</Grid>
```

### 4. Padding-only container

```tsx
import { Box } from '@appdirect/ds-prototype-kit';
<Box p="md" bg="gray.1">{children}</Box>
```

### 5. Centered content

```tsx
import { Center } from '@appdirect/ds-prototype-kit';
<Center h={200}>{children}</Center>
```

### 6. Page-level container

```tsx
import { Container } from '@appdirect/ds-prototype-kit';
<Container size="md">{children}</Container>
```

### 7. Advanced flex

```tsx
import { Flex } from '@appdirect/ds-prototype-kit';
<Flex direction={{ base: 'column', sm: 'row' }} gap="md">{children}</Flex>
```

### 8. Fallback

Use `Box` with Mantine system props.

## Spacing

| Figma | Token |
|-------|-------|
| 4px | `"xs"` |
| 8px | `"sm"` |
| 16px | `"md"` |
| 24px | `"lg"` |
| 32px | `"xl"` |
| 48px | `"xxl"` |

If a layer is explicitly named `Stack`, `Grid`, or `Inline`, honor that name.
